Z||000002||hobbitt||12-08-2001||09:26 PM||||all i can tell you is that i own one alot like the one on the right but it is older and has two box ends on the handle. my snap on dealer can only tell me that he can't get any and that they were basically limited edition. it seems like the cup itself is a duplicate of a socket used in airplanes or military vehicles. wish i knew more also but that is all he could tell me||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jake_Dragon||12-08-2001||09:27 PM||||Looks like your keeping up with them. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/guin.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/coffee.gif"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fleabitdog||12-09-2001||01:24 AM||||Hobbit<BR> They are both identical the one is fresh out of the freezer. I usually run water over them and put about 3/4" in the bottom and throw in freezer. Only thing to remember when you fill it with whatever drink you are having, make sure you run some water over where your lips are going to touch. So they don't freeze to the mug.<BR>Jake, Yes I use it quite often but mostly for pepsi. Years ago I got a noggin for xmas (pewter mug) It came with instructions on breakin in the noggin.  You fill it with beer and let it sit over night. Next day rinse with water and freeze. Never wash with soap. just rinse with water. That is why it is darker inside. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||hobbitt||12-09-2001||06:56 PM||||I gotta get a new digital camera but here is mine, mostly used as apencil holder on my desk. and no the mug is not bent in the second picture, like i said gotta get a new digital.bye the way in the first picture you can see the size of the socket!!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/somug1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/somug2.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||12-09-2001||07:07 PM||||You shouldn't really drink any type of acidic, or any other beverage for that matter, out of a pewter mug. Pewter is about 10% lead and 90% tin. Pewterware is best used for display only. You will ingest trace amounts of lead salts which accumulate over time.<BR>Eat, drink and be merry for tomorrow you may die.||||reg||1
